[{"input":"# Introduction\n\n## Who are we?\n\n* Lecturer: Col IMM Ben LAUWENS, PhD MScEng / D30.19 / [ben.lauwens@mil.be](mailto:ben.lauwens@mil.be)\n* Assistant: Mr Jean-François de KEMMETER, PhD MSc / D30.17 / [jean-francois.dekemmeter@mil.be](mailto:jean-francois.dekemmeter@mil.be)\n* Assistant: Maj Piet VAN DER PAELT, MSc / D30.25 / [piet.vanderpaelt@mil.be](mailto:piet.vanderpaelt@mil.be)\n\n## Course\n\n* Theory: 14 Hr → 42 Hr\n* Exercises: 18 Hr \t→ 36 Hr\n\n## Documentation\n\n* Handouts\n\n## Evaluations\n\n* Test: 05/11:\n    * Theory: 30 min - multiple choice without notes\n    * Exercises: 1Hr 30min - with Excel and notes\n\n* Exam:\n    * Theory: written exam - 1 Hr multiple choice without notes\n    * Exercises: written exam - 3 Hr with Excel and notes\n\n## Schedule\n\n|Lectures|Theory|Exercises|Topic|\n|:-------:|:-----:|:--------:|:---|\n|05/10|1||Introduction and Computing Concepts|\n|09/10|2-3||Digital Information and Digital Electronics|\n|12/10|4||Digital Logic and Memory|\n|16/10||1-2|Digital Information|\n|19/10|5||Computer Hardware and Architecture|\n|23/10||3-4|Digital Electronics and Digital Logics|\n|26/10||5|Memory|\n|30/10||6-7|Computer Harware and Architecture|\n|06/11|6-7||Software and Machine Instructions|\n|09/11|8||Software and Machine Instructions|\n|13/11||8-9|Software and Machine Instructions|\n|16/11||10|Software and Machine Instructions|\n|20/11|9-10||Algorithms and Programming Fundamentals |\n|23/11|11||Operating Systems |\n|27/11||11-12|Algorithms and Programming Fundamentals|\n|30/11|12||Computer Networks and the Internet|\n|04/12||13-14|Algorithms and Programming Fundamentals|\n|07/12|13||Cybersecurity and Cryptography|\n|11/12||15-16|Computer Networks and the Internet|\n|14/12|14||Generative Artificial Intelligence|\n|18/12||17-18|Cybersecurity and Cryptography|","output":"","result":"# Introduction\n\n## Who are we?\n\n* Lecturer: Col IMM Ben LAUWENS, PhD MScEng / D30.19 / [ben.lauwens@mil.be](mailto:ben.lauwens@mil.be)\